the synergy between character classes is  one of the things that makes the battle  against hordes of xenomorphs exciting in  aliens fire team elite with the start of  the game's first live content season  developer cold iron is adding a new  brand of marine to the battlefield the  phalanx class we got a chance to go  hands-on with the phanlance ahead of its  release to see what it adds to your  fireteam if you like this video and you  want to see more coverage of aliens  fireteam elite go ahead and hit the like  and subscribe buttons  as the name suggests the phalanx marine  sports a deployable shield that turns it  into a frontline fighter acting as your  team's tank the shield can block melee  damage and incoming shots allowing you  to better survive some close encounters  with both alien enemies and the  synthetic soldiers that populate the  campaign it's a trooper that's great for  drawing fire and drawing a crowd so the  rest of your three-player squad can  avoid being overwhelmed and pick off  enemies with a little more space to  breathe the phalanx's primary ability is  a shield you can toggle on or off  there's no cooldown on this thing when  you pull the shield out it allows you to  absorb attacks without getting hurt so  long as they're coming from in front of  you that incentivizes you to hold down  choke points and wade into narrow  corridors attacks from the side or  behind acid damage and some explosions  will still hurt but for the most part if  you can funnel your attackers into a  place where you can only fight them head  on you can block their attacks and blow  them apart with a shotgun your passive  ability bulwark increases the damage  your weapons do for every attack you  block with your shield so there's a big  incentive to try to keep it deployed as  much as possible  using the phalanx shield can be pretty  effective but it comes with drawbacks  first you can only use handguns and  close quarters weapons with this class  since you only have one hand to operate  your guns you can use them from behind  your shield but you lose the ability to  move quickly while the shield is  deployed that can make it tough to  respond to threats coming at you from  the sides or behind but sprinting or  dodging automatically folds the shield  up making it possible to quickly escape  when something like a xenomorph warrior  comes roaring at you  controlling crowds and keeping enemy  attention is the phalanx is back and  your second ability is the shock pulse  it stuns enemies in a radius around you  making it great for those moments when  you're unexpectedly surrounded and your  shield isn't helping the shock pulse  also dishes out damage over time and can  be tweaked to either hit enemies harder  with that initial blast or stun them  more effectively coupled with the shield  the ability is great for allowing you to  walk into danger and take lots of  enemies out of the fight at once so you  and your team can mop them up before  they become a problem aliens fire team  elite works to toe the line between  making you feel like a badass but one  who knows that the situation you're  fighting through could go badly at any  second having the shield is great but it  won't stop everything coming at you you  can block some but probably not all  explosive damage with the shield and it  won't keep acid from messing up your  feet should you walk through some it  also won't protect you from enemies that  grab you like the warrior or the prowler  you still need to keep your head on a  swivel and when things get rough you'll  sometimes need to stow the shield and  get out of harm's way just like the  other classes do as with all the classes  in aliens fireteam elite the phan links  is best used in conjunction with a  diverse fire team backing you up its  ability to tank damage and zap several  enemies at once are great when paired  with the dock class which can throw down  a trauma station to keep the phalanx  healed to absorb even more punishment a  high damage class like the demolisher or  gunner is a good addition for killing  enemies quickly to make sure the phalanx  doesn't become overwhelmed as the  phalanx we found it was very easy to  find yourself thinking you're in better  shape than you are and to be so focused  on dealing with one set of enemies that  you forget about another set coming up  on your flank the phalanx class is free  to all aliens fire team elite players  and is part of the game's first content  season which kicks off on september 8th  the season also includes several new  weapons you can earn in-game including a  laser pistol modeled after weapons seen  in the original alien and a new assault  rifle minigun and sniper rifle if you  want to see more of what i'm talking  about here's gameplay of the phalanx in  action as we take on xenomorphs and the  weyland yutani synthetics in alien fire  team elites second campaign giants in  the earth  ain't over till it's over they get sit  tight  [Music]  [Music]  [Music]  approach  must have heard the gunfire  should not be capable of this  [Music]  oh  [Music]  [Music]  shut down  [Music]  so  so  so  [Music]  is  the computers here are protected by 16  million character ciphers  esther seal the door behind them catch  your breath fire team rodriguez is just  ahead
 

